Looks names up over IPv6 as glibc does (ADR 0332). mlibc asked only IPv4
nameservers, asked AF_UNSPEC lookups for A records alone, gave the
addresses in the order found, failed AF_INET6 lookups that AI_V4MAPPED
should have answered, and took AI_ADDRCONFIG's narrowing for the family
asked even when one was. Now:
  - nameservers may be IPv6 ones, on a link with their interface after
    a %, as fe80::1%net0 or fe80::1%2 (RFC 4007);
  - AF_UNSPEC asks for A and AAAA records, and gethostbyname for A ones;
  - getaddrinfo orders what it found as RFC 6724's destination address
    selection does (rules 1, 2, 5, 6, 8 and 9, with its default policy
    table), when IPv6 addresses are among them, learning each one's
    source address by connecting a UDP socket, as glibc and musl do;
  - AF_INET6 with AI_V4MAPPED gives a name's IPv4 addresses, mapped,
    when it has no IPv6 ones;
  - AI_ADDRCONFIG narrows AF_UNSPEC to the family the machine has
    addresses of, and fails AF_INET or AF_INET6 when it has none of
    that family, as glibc does.
Meant for upstream.

